title: Tackle Definition Packages Tasks
status: draft
created: 2026-10-21
author: adrian
items[18]{id,title,description,criteria,complexity,effort,dependencies,refs}:
  T-001,"[x] Extend the definition type for packages","Add an optional package directory and a sorted resource listing to Definition. Enumerate resources as paths relative to the package directory, excluding the entry point, with a stable sort so the listing and the lock hash are deterministic.","Unit tests: a directory definition reports its directory and sorted resources; a flat definition reports no directory and an empty listing; resource enumeration is order-stable.",medium,"2-3h",,"definition-packages"
  T-002,"[x] Directory definition discovery","Extend the loader to scan .agentkit/tackle/<kind>/ for directory definitions at <name>/<ENTRY>.md, dispatching on the per-kind entry point name PROMPT.md, PERSONA.md, or ACTOR.md. A directory whose entry point is missing or misnamed is a load error naming the path. Size caps apply to the package total.","Unit tests: directory definitions of every kind load; a missing entry point and a misnamed entry point each error naming the path; an oversized package is rejected.",medium,"3-4h","T-001","definition-packages,entry-point-convention"
  T-003,"[x] Repository-only definitions and flat compatibility","Remove the user configuration layer for personas, actors, and prompts so definitions load only from the repository tree, and keep flat single-file definitions loading unchanged for definitions without resources. A flat and a directory definition of the same name in one kind directory is a load error naming both paths. Built-in defaults remain flat embedded assets at the lowest precedence.","Unit tests: a definition directory under the user config dir is ignored; a flat definition still loads; a flat and directory collision errors naming both paths; a discovered definition replaces the built-in and is surfaced.",medium,"3-4h","T-002","location-discovery,built-in-definitions,backward-compatibility"
  T-004,"[x] Context variable substitution","Add the $ namespace to prompt expansion. $.name is the definition name and $.dir is the repository-relative package directory. Invokable::Prompt carries the definition directory and resource listing so expand_user and expand_model substitute and append without reaching back into the definitions map. Bare parameter names remain the parameter form.","Unit tests: {{ $.dir }} and {{ $.name }} substitute; a declared parameter named dir does not collide with {{ $.dir }}; a flat definition yields an empty $.dir.",medium,"2-4h","T-001","context-variables"
  T-005,"[x] Resource listing for prompts","Append the resource listing to the expanded body of a prompt, after substitution, so the model knows which paths under $.dir it may read. A prompt with no resources gets no listing.","Unit tests: an expanded prompt body ends with its sorted resource listing; a resource-less prompt is unchanged.",low,"1-2h","T-004","resource-listing"
  T-006,"[x] Context variables and listing for personas","Substitute context variables into persona bodies and append the persona resource listing when the system prompt is assembled, sharing one implementation with prompt expansion so the two cannot diverge. Actors carry no body and are unaffected.","Unit tests: a persona body substitutes $.dir and $.name and gains its listing before the invokable manifest; an actor produces no listing.",low,"1-2h","T-004","context-variables,resource-listing"
  T-007,"[x] Manifest parsing","Parse .agentkit/tackle/definitions.toml into sources and selections. Each [[source]] declares a required kind with no default and a kind-named spec table: git with url plus optional ref and path, or path with dir. Selections under [definitions.<source>] are keyed by kind with a list of names. The url field also accepts the PEP 508 git+ URL form, parsed into url, ref, and subdirectory.","Unit tests: both source kinds parse; the PEP 508 git+ form parses into url, ref, and subdirectory; a source without kind is a parse error naming the source.",medium,"3-4h",,"definitions-manifest,source-specifications"
  T-008,"[x] Manifest validation invariants","Enforce the manifest invariants at parse time: unique local definition names across the resolved set, source and definition paths confined to their roots, and no override of a delegated or local name. Violations are parse errors naming the offending source and definition.","Unit tests: a duplicate name across sources errors; a path escaping the source root errors; a definition path escaping the repository errors; a valid manifest parses.",medium,"2-3h","T-007","definitions-manifest,source-specifications"
  T-009,"[x] Manifest delegation","Resolve [[extends]] entries transitively: fetch each delegated definitions.toml at its pinned revision, union-merge its sources and selections with the local manifest, and treat duplicate names anywhere in the resolved set as a parse error. No override is permitted.","Unit tests: a delegated manifest contributes its definitions; nested extends resolve; a duplicate between local and delegated errors; a cycle is detected and errors.",high,"4-6h","T-007","manifest-delegation"
  T-010,"[x] Lock schema and package hashing","Read and write .agentkit/tackle/definitions.lock: each source resolved to an immutable commit, each definition to a content hash over its sorted files (relative path plus length plus bytes). A flat definition hashes as bare file content so existing records stay stable. The lock carries integrity only and never gates loading.","Unit tests: a lock round-trips; package hashing is stable across file order and changes when any file changes; a flat definition hashes as its file content.",medium,"3-4h","T-001","lock-file"
  T-011,"[x] Git source resolution","Resolve git sources through git2: clone or fetch the url, check out the requested ref, and resolve it to a commit. Reuse the existing git2 dependency; add no new dependency. An unreachable or unresolvable source fails with the source name and URL.","Integration tests against a local git fixture: a tag, a branch, and a commit ref each resolve to the expected commit; an unknown ref errors naming the source.",medium,"3-4h","T-007","source-specifications,minimal-dependencies"
  T-012,"[x] Path source resolution and vendoring","Resolve kind = path sources from the local filesystem and vendor selected definitions from both source kinds into the repository tree at .agentkit/tackle/<kind>/<name>/. Vendoring writes the entry point and all resources and reports the definition paths it produced.","Integration tests: a local path source vendors a definition with resources into the tree; a git source vendors the same; the tree matches the source files.",medium,"3-4h","T-010,T-011","source-specifications,definitions-cli"
  T-013,"[x] Vendoring pipeline and fail-closed behaviour","Wire get and update: get resolves the manifest against the lock and vendors the locked revisions, update re-resolves refs, re-vendors, and rewrites the lock. Both are the only network operations. A failure at any point leaves the tree and lock unchanged.","Integration tests: get reproduces the locked revisions; update advances them and rewrites the lock; an unreachable source leaves the tree and lock byte-identical.",high,"4-6h","T-009,T-012","definitions-cli,fail-closed,determinism"
  T-014,"[x] Definitions subcommand surface","Add the tackle definitions subcommand with the def alias: init scaffolds a manifest, add and remove edit selections, get and update drive the vendoring pipeline, and list reports declared and vendored definitions with status. The loader remains independent of the manifest and lock.","CLI tests: definitions and def are equivalent; init writes a parseable manifest; add and remove update selections; list reports declared and vendored definitions.",medium,"3-4h","T-013","definitions-cli,loader-independence"
  T-015,"[x] Verify drift detection","Implement verify: re-hash each vendored package and compare against the lock, reporting drift for any package whose files changed and exiting non-zero. A missing or stale lock is an error naming tackle definitions get.","Tests: editing any file in a package makes verify report that package and exit non-zero; an unmodified tree verifies clean; a missing lock errors naming get.",medium,"2-3h","T-014,T-010","loader-independence,fail-closed"
  T-016,"[x] Retire per-file definition trust","Remove the per-path TOFU trust record for definitions now that they are repository-resident. Definition bodies and resources load without a prompt; bounded Rhai scripts also load because the engine limits are the consent.","Tests: definitions and bounded scripts load in a repository with no consent prompt; the per-path trust entries for definitions are no longer written.",medium,"2-4h","T-003","trust-boundary"
  T-017,"[x] Project-scope host execution denial","Deny unbounded host execution at project scope: mcp_servers, client_tools, endpoints, and credential_helper declared in project configuration are ignored, and are honoured only from user configuration outside the repository. Preserve the existing hard denials.","Tests: a project-declared mcp_servers entry and client_tools entry are ignored; endpoints and credential_helper remain rejected at project scope; the same entries load from user configuration.",high,"3-5h","T-016","trust-boundary,security-posture"
  T-018,"[x] Reconcile security and tackle documentation","Update security.mdx to state the sandbox-boundary posture and remove the per-entry consent description, and amend the tackle ADR FR-022 and AC-010 to record repository-only definitions and the retired trust gate.","security.mdx describes the boundary posture with no per-entry consent; the tackle ADR records the amendments; no doc references the retired per-file definition trust.",low,"1-2h","T-017","trust-boundary"
